<title>GREECE: TABLE OF GREEK MUTUAL FUND FLOWS, ASSETS.</title>
<headline>TABLE OF GREEK MUTUAL FUND FLOWS, ASSETS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ionian Bank reported the</p>
<p>following daily and year-to-date changes in the volume of Greek</p>
<p>mutual fund outstanding shares, net assets and net share prices,</p>
<p>as well as total net asset sizes as of May 28.</p>
<p>				    May 28/May 27   May 28/Dec 31, 96</p>
<p>						 (%)		  (%)</p>
<p>NET SHARE PRICES*</p>
<p>  Total market			    0.06		 6.91</p>
<p>  Fixed income &amp;money market funds  0.03		 4.99</p>
<p>  International funds		   0.25		 9.92</p>
<p>  Growth Funds			    0.53		61.13</p>
<p>* Prices include distributed dividends</p>
<p>VOLUME OF SHARES</p>
<p>  Total market			   -0.26		31.48</p>
<p>  Fixed income &amp;money market funds -0.30		32.08</p>
<p>  International funds		   0.05		10.23</p>
<p>  Growth funds			    0.74		27.38</p>
<p>NET ASSETS</p>
<p>  Total market			   -0.19		38.84</p>
<p>  Fixed income &amp;money market funds -0.27		37.17</p>
<p>  International funds		   0.32		18.74</p>
<p>  Growth funds			    1.24	     100.83</p>
<p>All calculations are based on a performance index of mutual</p>
<p>funds whose base was set to be equal to 100 on December 31,</p>
<p>1991.</p>
<p>NET ASSET SIZES (in drachmas)</p>
<p>  Total market				  5,280,189,564,352</p>
<p>  Fixed income funds			  1,916,245,896,495</p>
<p>  Money market funds			  3,024,218,440,111</p>
<p>  International funds			    93,347,129,040</p>
<p>  Growth funds				    246,378,098,706</p>
<p>--Angelos Kiosklis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
